Third-party components
-----------------------

- Vue (vue, vue-router)
  https://github.com/vuejs/core
  https://github.com/vuejs/router
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Used for: the reactive component model and the client-side router
  (hash history, so the console works under any sub-path on the router).

- Vite (@vitejs/plugin-vite equivalent plugin, unplugin-vue-components,
  unplugin-vue-components/resolvers)
  https://github.com/vitejs/vite
  https://github.com/unplugin/unplugin-vue-components
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Used for: the build tool and the on-demand import of Element Plus
  components and their stylesheets.

- TypeScript
  https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  Used for: the type system of the whole frontend.

- Element Plus
  https://github.com/element-plus/element-plus
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Used for: the UI component library (forms, tables, dialogs, selects,
  switches, message boxes). Imported on demand; no component stylesheet is
  vendored into this repository.

- Apache ECharts
  https://github.com/apache/echarts
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  Used for: the line charts on the dashboard and the monitoring pages.
  Only the line chart is registered.

- Lucide (lucide-vue-next)
  https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide
  Licensed under the ISC License.
  Used for: the icon set of the interface.

- art-design-pro
  https://github.com/Daymychen/art-design-pro
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Used for: the visual baseline of the design tokens. This project's design
  tokens are derived from it -- the gray ramp, the background/box colors and
  the border color in src/styles/tokens.css map one-to-one onto art-design-pro's
  --art-gray-* and --default-* custom properties (see the token-by-token table
  in third-party/art-design-pro/UPSTREAM.md). Tailwind is not used; the tokens
  were re-declared as plain CSS custom properties, with the contrast ratios
  measured against this project's own palette.
  Distribution: **yes** -- a verbatim snapshot is vendored in this repository
  under third-party/art-design-pro/ at commit
  f3aaf58eec1a0e988f162352c33862327a484f95 (2026-06-01). The upstream LICENSE
  is kept alongside it, and not one byte of upstream source was modified.
  It is a design reference, not a runtime dependency: the frontend never
  imports anything from that directory.

- OpenWrt / LuCI
  https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt
  https://github.com/openwrt/luci
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  Used for: the target platform. This project calls the rpcd/ubus interfaces
  and the LuCI-rpc object that OpenWrt already exposes; it contains no
  OpenWrt or LuCI source code. LuCI is kept only as an emergency entry point
  on the device.
  Distribution: **no** -- neither repository is vendored here. Both are far
  above the 5 MB vendoring threshold, and this project only calls their
  interfaces. See third-party/README.md for the full decision record.

